{
	"itemName": "NSLOCTEXT(\"\", \"A09DD9B747FF3320003ECABBE80B7578\", \"Pridestrider\")",
	"description": "NSLOCTEXT(\"[D20C99C24B2FABB4DC05E3BF1EE067C5]\", \"6B395C3F41B6EB7FDF9AD4A85AD456CE\", \"Flying Mount\\r\\nLevel 25\\r\\n\\r\\n165% Ground Speed\\r\\n215% Flying Speed\\r\\n500% Maximum Health\")",
	"use": "",
	"details": "",
	"flavor": "NSLOCTEXT(\"[D20C99C24B2FABB4DC05E3BF1EE067C5]\", \"70F0A94C4F6E499F60D9F68D9005D1F7\", \"The Pridestrider moves with the solemn grace of a living myth, a mount woven from the breath of storms and the silence of sacred groves. Its head bears the visage of a white lion, regal and unyielding, crowned with a pair of straight, gleaming horns that rise like spears of moonstone toward the heavens. The torso is that of a great gorilla, heavy with primal strength and steady as a mountain?s heart. Its wings, vast and fragile in appearance, unfold in shimmering layers like the breath of a butterfly caught between worlds, scattering iridescent light with each beat. The Pridestrider does not gallop or glide but commands the air with the authority of a sovereign spirit. It answers only to the Mayor of Azmaran, whose dominion must hold the weight of law and the lightness of vision in equal measure.\")",
